    "result": "I implemented `search_products` in `solution.py`. I haven't run it or any tests, as instructed.\n\nIt validates `order_by`, `limit` and `offset` first and raises `ValueError` if any is invalid. It then runs a single read-only SELECT that filters on `stock > 0` and the optional `max_price`, and returns dicts with `id`, `name` and `price`.\n\n- **Substring match:** it uses `instr(lower(name), lower(?))`, so `%` and `_` are matched literally and case-folding is ASCII-only. An empty string skips the filter.\n- **Ordering:** the query orders by the chosen column in the chosen direction, then by `id` ascending as the tie-break, and applies `LIMIT` and `OFFSET` after that.\n- **Bool values:** `True` and `False` are rejected as `limit` or `offset` values, since Python treats them as integers.",
